1
00:00:02,160 --> 00:00:05,540
<i>[Jeon Yeo Been]</i>

2
00:00:06,670 --> 00:00:09,770
<i>[Jin Young]</i>

3
00:00:11,010 --> 00:00:14,040
<i>[Seo Hyun Woo]</i>

4
00:00:16,570 --> 00:00:19,500
<i>[Jang Yoon Ju]</i>

5
00:00:20,750 --> 00:00:23,760
<i>[Joo Hyun Young]</i>

6
00:00:26,410 --> 00:00:28,170
<i>[Moon Sung Keun]</i>

7
00:00:34,620 --> 00:00:40,070
🤫<i>Ms. Incognito</i>🎭

8
00:00:41,967 --> 00:00:45,040
<i>[This drama is fiction. Any resemblance
to real people or events is coincidental.]</i>

9
00:00:46,033 --> 00:00:48,100
<i>[Episode 10]</i>

10
00:00:50,010 --> 00:01:00,020
<i>Timing and subtitles by the</i> 👠 Se Mi Secrets 🕶️ <i>Team @viki.com</i>

11
00:01:37,667 --> 00:01:39,067
Here.

12
00:01:48,600 --> 00:01:51,133
Still trying to earn good karma?

13
00:01:52,333 --> 00:01:55,700
I'm here thanks to that, together with you.

14
00:01:59,300 --> 00:02:01,767
What's so special about this place?

15
00:02:05,600 --> 00:02:10,033
Then why are you here?

16
00:02:12,767 --> 00:02:19,633
Yeong Ran, after you returned from Muchang,

17
00:02:19,633 --> 00:02:21,567
it feels like you've changed.

18
00:02:21,567 --> 00:02:24,933
You used to be indifferent
and not care about people.

19
00:02:28,133 --> 00:02:29,833
You...

20
00:02:30,767 --> 00:02:34,733
like that guy from earlier, don't you?

21
00:02:50,400 --> 00:02:53,167
I shouldn't like him.

22
00:02:58,300 --> 00:03:02,067
What do you mean you shouldn't like him?

23
00:03:02,067 --> 00:03:05,933
How could it be wrong to like another person?

24
00:03:15,433 --> 00:03:18,667
He's such a good person.

25
00:03:21,967 --> 00:03:24,667
That's exactly why I shouldn't like him.

26
00:03:49,333 --> 00:03:51,267
Have you eaten?

27
00:03:52,367 --> 00:03:53,960
Yes.

28
00:03:54,500 --> 00:03:56,333
Thank you.

29
00:03:57,933 --> 00:04:00,133
Why did you come back?

30
00:04:01,300 --> 00:04:05,167
Didn't you come to Seoul to meet Ms. Bu Se Mi?

31
00:04:05,867 --> 00:04:07,867
That's why I came.

32
00:04:08,567 --> 00:04:10,933
<i>Those feelings are</i>

33
00:04:10,933 --> 00:04:13,367
<i>only mistaken delusions.</i>

34
00:04:14,000 --> 00:04:15,633
<i>Also,</i>

35
00:04:16,167 --> 00:04:20,000
<i>I don't like you enough to abandon
my dreams, Mr. Jeon Dong Min.</i>

36
00:04:22,133 --> 00:04:24,333
How is Ms. Bu doing?

37
00:04:24,333 --> 00:04:29,167
All they mentioned on the news was Ms. Bu.

38
00:04:33,067 --> 00:04:35,167
The news says

39
00:04:35,700 --> 00:04:38,800
Ms. Yeong Ran is a bad person,

40
00:04:40,733 --> 00:04:44,867
but actually, she's a good person,

41
00:04:47,100 --> 00:04:50,500
afraid that someone might get hurt due to her,

42
00:04:50,500 --> 00:04:53,133
she's enduring everything alone.

43
00:04:55,767 --> 00:04:57,933
So did you get rejected?

44
00:05:02,433 --> 00:05:05,133
You always nail such guesses.

45
00:05:12,667 --> 00:05:14,200
Tae Min.

46
00:05:14,200 --> 00:05:15,633
Yes?

47
00:05:16,467 --> 00:05:18,200
I...

48
00:05:20,733 --> 00:05:23,733
I can't do anything for her.

49
00:05:24,700 --> 00:05:27,733
Why can't you do anything?

50
00:05:28,267 --> 00:05:32,267
Just being there for her
when she's struggling helps so much.

51
00:05:33,400 --> 00:05:37,433
That's why I'm staying by Hye Ji's side.

52
00:05:40,967 --> 00:05:42,567
Right.

53
00:05:43,833 --> 00:05:45,433
Dong Min.

54
00:05:47,900 --> 00:05:52,100
They say you need stamina
to properly support your person.

55
00:05:52,100 --> 00:05:56,867
That's why ICU patients' families all exercise.

56
00:05:56,867 --> 00:06:00,767
Just mirror my movements, okay?

57
00:06:00,767 --> 00:06:03,000
It'll clear your mind too.

58
00:06:03,000 --> 00:06:06,267
Let's start with push-ups.

59
00:06:06,267 --> 00:06:07,900
Here I go.

60
00:06:15,030 --> 00:06:17,367
Jeon Dong Min, fighting!

61
00:06:19,067 --> 00:06:20,800
Thank you.

62
00:06:26,367 --> 00:06:29,267
Good morning, Madam.

63
00:06:29,267 --> 00:06:31,900
Do you have plans today?

64
00:06:31,900 --> 00:06:33,300
Yes.

65
00:06:41,967 --> 00:06:43,333
Who is it?

66
00:06:43,333 --> 00:06:45,267
It's the police.

67
00:06:46,733 --> 00:06:50,667
They say they're the police, Madam.

68
00:06:50,667 --> 00:06:52,400
What should we do?

69
00:06:52,400 --> 00:06:54,467
Please open the door.

70
00:06:56,667 --> 00:06:58,567
Madam.

71
00:07:02,633 --> 00:07:04,367
Ms. Kim Yeong Ran,

72
00:07:05,733 --> 00:07:09,900
you're under arrest for conspiracy
to murder Ga Seon Yeong.

73
00:07:14,967 --> 00:07:18,133
Is it necessary to handcuff me?

74
00:07:18,133 --> 00:07:22,067
We make exception
with no risk of escape or assault.

75
00:07:22,067 --> 00:07:23,733
I don't plan on doing either.

76
00:07:23,733 --> 00:07:25,433
I'll go on my own.

77
00:07:25,433 --> 00:07:27,233
All right then.

78
00:07:38,333 --> 00:07:39,800
Attorney.

79
00:07:39,800 --> 00:07:41,600
What should I do?

80
00:07:42,800 --> 00:07:43,833
<i>The phone is off...</i>

81
00:07:43,833 --> 00:07:47,567
Why is Attorney Lee's phone off
at a time like this?

82
00:07:48,800 --> 00:07:50,533
<i>The phone is off...</i>

83
00:07:50,533 --> 00:07:52,667
Attorney.

84
00:07:55,333 --> 00:07:57,767
Without Attorney Lee, Kim Yeong Ran
will be investigated alone,

85
00:07:57,767 --> 00:08:02,000
and since we submitted evidence,
she can't easily get out of this.

86
00:08:02,000 --> 00:08:04,333
The end is in sight, Professor.

87
00:08:04,333 --> 00:08:07,100
Prepare for next week's board meeting flawlessly.

88
00:08:07,100 --> 00:08:08,767
Understood.

89
00:08:14,300 --> 00:08:17,450
<i>[Seo-gu Police Station]</i>

90
00:08:17,967 --> 00:08:20,233
There's Kim Yeong Ran.

91
00:08:20,233 --> 00:08:22,633
Ms. Kim Yeong Ran, did you really order
Professor Ga Seon Yeong's murder?

92
00:08:22,633 --> 00:08:25,433
Is it true this was done for inheritance disputes?

93
00:08:31,600 --> 00:08:34,433
That's right. Yes.

94
00:08:53,033 --> 00:08:55,000
Okay.

95
00:09:16,810 --> 00:09:23,120
<i>[Private Investigation]</i>

96
00:09:39,300 --> 00:09:41,467
There we go.

97
00:09:41,467 --> 00:09:43,433
Zero, three, five, six...

98
00:09:48,400 --> 00:09:50,600
Eight, two, eight, two...

99
00:09:53,800 --> 00:09:56,133
These pathetic fools.

100
00:10:02,008 --> 00:10:03,467
<i>[Byeol Nae (11 calls)]</i>

101
00:10:03,467 --> 00:10:06,733
What? Why did she make so many calls?

102
00:10:08,267 --> 00:10:11,167
<i>[Attorney! Yeong Ran is getting
arrested by the police!]</i>

103
00:10:11,167 --> 00:10:13,267
<i>[Where are you?]</i>

104
00:10:19,267 --> 00:10:23,567
<i>[Is the motive an inheritance dispute? Ms. Kim,
suspected to have ordered assault on step-daughter]</i>

105
00:10:23,567 --> 00:10:25,833
<i>[Ms. Kim, heir to Gaseong Group,
arrested for Professor Ga Seon Yeong's attempted murder]</i>

106
00:10:25,833 --> 00:10:27,367
Gosh. See?

107
00:10:27,367 --> 00:10:29,733
She can't do without me.

108
00:10:54,560 --> 00:10:58,700
Excuse me, I need to use
the bathroom; my stomach hurts.

109
00:10:58,700 --> 00:11:02,533
<i>Do your business right there, Esteemed Attorney.</i>

110
00:11:05,167 --> 00:11:08,267
- Did you give him a chamber pot?
- I gave him a newspaper.

111
00:11:08,267 --> 00:11:11,067
Jeez, it'll start to stink.

112
00:11:11,067 --> 00:11:13,967
- I'll handle it later.
- Whatever. You clean it all up, Hyung.

113
00:11:13,967 --> 00:11:16,133
Darn it.

114
00:11:23,200 --> 00:11:25,600
<i>[Private Investigation]</i>

115
00:11:27,833 --> 00:11:30,067
I have a fear of heights.

116
00:11:30,067 --> 00:11:31,967
Ga Seon Yeong!

117
00:12:06,867 --> 00:12:08,867
- Wait.
- Darn it.

118
00:12:08,867 --> 00:12:11,800
We taped his mouth; how is he talking?

119
00:12:13,300 --> 00:12:15,133
Darn it.

120
00:12:15,133 --> 00:12:16,967
Darn it, hurry up.

121
00:12:16,967 --> 00:12:19,733
<i>Do it fast.</i>

122
00:12:20,700 --> 00:12:23,433
What are you doing?

123
00:12:29,550 --> 00:12:31,920
Hey!

124
00:12:36,367 --> 00:12:38,833
- Hey!
- Hey, you punk!

125
00:12:51,433 --> 00:12:53,767
<i>[Seo-gu Police Station]</i>

126
00:13:02,767 --> 00:13:05,300
Yeong Ran.

127
00:13:09,033 --> 00:13:12,333
<i>Yeong Ran.</i>

128
00:13:21,033 --> 00:13:23,633
<i>Hey, Yeong Ran! Kim Yeong Ran!</i>

129
00:13:29,533 --> 00:13:32,467
<i>Where are you?</i>

130
00:13:33,167 --> 00:13:35,267
<i>Are you there?</i>

131
00:13:45,033 --> 00:13:47,500
See you again, Yeong Ran.

132
00:13:59,667 --> 00:14:02,800
Excuse me, I need to use the restroom.

133
00:14:02,800 --> 00:14:05,133
Yes, come this way.

134
00:14:50,760 --> 00:14:52,633
<i>[Bank Transfer Statement]</i>

135
00:14:52,633 --> 00:14:54,733
Here's the bank transfer statement
showing ₩50 million ($35,000)

136
00:14:54,733 --> 00:14:58,367
transferred from your account
to Kim Gyo Bong's account.

137
00:14:59,333 --> 00:15:05,567
You're the one who paid to have
Professor Ga Seon Yeong murdered, right?

138
00:15:05,567 --> 00:15:09,267
My mother, Kim So Yeong, has my ID and seal.

139
00:15:09,267 --> 00:15:11,800
She has three criminal records
for running a pyramid scheme.

140
00:15:11,800 --> 00:15:13,533
She used my bank account for that.

141
00:15:13,533 --> 00:15:15,767
Have you investigated this?

142
00:15:15,767 --> 00:15:18,367
Answer only the questions I ask.

143
00:15:18,367 --> 00:15:21,167
Are you the daughter of Kim Gyo Bong's
common-law wife?

144
00:15:21,167 --> 00:15:24,900
- Did he say I told him to do it?
- I'll be the one asking questions.

145
00:15:24,900 --> 00:15:27,400
You are acquainted with Kim Gyo Bong, right?

146
00:15:27,967 --> 00:15:31,867
I'll meet Kim Gyo Bong myself.

147
00:15:35,367 --> 00:15:37,033
You're in front of the police station, right?

148
00:15:37,033 --> 00:15:38,550
- Which police station is it?
<i>- Seo-gu Police Station.</i>

149
00:15:38,550 --> 00:15:40,860
"Seo-gu"? Got it.

150
00:15:42,667 --> 00:15:45,067
He's still the same.

151
00:15:46,000 --> 00:15:49,333
<i>But her lawyer's not with her?</i>

152
00:15:51,700 --> 00:15:54,533
You told me to do it, Yeong Ran.

153
00:15:54,533 --> 00:15:56,900
Why do you pretend not to know?

154
00:15:58,100 --> 00:15:59,833
Detective.

155
00:16:00,767 --> 00:16:03,833
Kim Yeong Ran here

156
00:16:03,833 --> 00:16:06,400
ordered Professor Ga Seon Yeong's murder.

157
00:16:06,400 --> 00:16:10,700
She gave me ₩50 million and promised
₩100 million more if I succeeded.

158
00:16:10,700 --> 00:16:14,700
But when I failed, she pretended not to know.

159
00:16:15,500 --> 00:16:17,767
So I turned myself in.

160
00:16:19,933 --> 00:16:22,400
I have nothing more to say.

161
00:16:23,633 --> 00:16:25,667
I have evidence to submit.

162
00:16:25,667 --> 00:16:27,500
What kind of evidence?

163
00:16:28,633 --> 00:16:30,600
Evidence proving my innocence.

164
00:16:30,600 --> 00:16:33,767
Wait, wait, Detective.

165
00:16:34,533 --> 00:16:37,200
Oh, these are all lies.

166
00:16:37,200 --> 00:16:40,733
She's the one who ordered it. There's evidence.

167
00:16:43,367 --> 00:16:46,467
You're just as cheeky as in childhood.

168
00:16:46,467 --> 00:16:49,067
I should just...

169
00:16:52,200 --> 00:16:55,667
It seems you still couldn't
erase that dirty habit.

170
00:16:56,933 --> 00:17:00,067
I'm not the child who used
to be beaten by you anymore.

171
00:17:01,367 --> 00:17:03,200
- You, darn it!
- Mr. Kim Gyo Bong!

172
00:17:03,200 --> 00:17:05,133
Hey.

173
00:17:05,133 --> 00:17:07,100
Sit down.

174
00:17:07,100 --> 00:17:09,600
Sit down!

175
00:17:09,600 --> 00:17:11,933
Oh, sure.

176
00:17:22,967 --> 00:17:25,600
<i>Kim Gyo Bong was recently released, right?</i>

177
00:17:25,600 --> 00:17:30,533
<i>He had no money and no job
so he eagerly took the bait I threw.</i>

178
00:17:31,167 --> 00:17:33,333
<i>I made him do it.</i>

179
00:17:33,333 --> 00:17:37,600
<i>Getting him to do the job
must have cost you a lot.</i>

180
00:17:37,600 --> 00:17:39,533
<i>Where would you get that kind of money?</i>

181
00:17:39,533 --> 00:17:41,230
<i>The money came from another source.</i>

182
00:17:41,230 --> 00:17:44,260
<i>I just played the middleman.</i>

183
00:17:44,260 --> 00:17:48,300
<i>Is Yeong Ran like they said on the news?</i>

184
00:17:50,600 --> 00:17:53,733
<i>Do you think she would give me a single won?</i>

185
00:17:54,500 --> 00:17:58,700
<i>She left me at the police station
and said I'm not her mother.</i>

186
00:17:58,700 --> 00:18:01,000
<i>That wench.</i>

187
00:18:01,000 --> 00:18:02,900
I submit this recording as evidence.

188
00:18:02,900 --> 00:18:04,533
No, no.

189
00:18:04,533 --> 00:18:07,700
These are all lies.

190
00:18:07,700 --> 00:18:11,833
- What kind of joke is this?
- Stay still, Mr. Kim Gyo Bong!

191
00:18:12,930 --> 00:18:17,167
We will verify the recording's authenticity today.

192
00:18:17,167 --> 00:18:19,433
Let's conclude today's inquiry here.

193
00:18:19,433 --> 00:18:23,267
You're not fully cleared of suspicion yet.

194
00:18:23,267 --> 00:18:27,467
You must promptly comply
if we request further investigation.

195
00:18:28,267 --> 00:18:30,233
Understood.

196
00:18:31,033 --> 00:18:33,733
Hey, Kim Yeong Ran, you've grown up, haven't you?

197
00:18:33,733 --> 00:18:37,667
I should have beaten you to death back then

198
00:18:37,667 --> 00:18:40,633
to shut you up for good. Hey.

199
00:18:40,633 --> 00:18:44,533
So you married a rich old man
and now you fear nothing, yes?

200
00:18:44,533 --> 00:18:48,500
You're right. I guess nothing is to fear now.

201
00:18:48,500 --> 00:18:50,567
Mr. Kim Gyo Bong.

202
00:18:55,200 --> 00:18:58,233
Do you know how long I've waited for this moment?

203
00:18:58,233 --> 00:19:00,267
Child abuse statute of limitation may have passed,

204
00:19:00,267 --> 00:19:03,567
but you'll pay dearly
for attempted murder and perjury,

205
00:19:03,567 --> 00:19:06,033
you piece of trash.

206
00:19:06,967 --> 00:19:09,167
- Hey!
- Kim Gyo Bong.

207
00:19:09,167 --> 00:19:12,933
You should pay for it!

208
00:19:12,933 --> 00:19:17,367
Ensure the recording Kim Yeong Ran
submitted isn't accepted as evidence

209
00:19:18,200 --> 00:19:20,533
and cut all loose ends.

210
00:19:24,833 --> 00:19:27,200
Impressive, Kim Yeong Ran.

211
00:19:27,867 --> 00:19:31,467
<i>[Seo-gu Police Station]</i>

212
00:19:35,467 --> 00:19:39,733
You were investigated as the mastermind
behind Professor Ga Seon Yeong's assault, right?

213
00:19:39,733 --> 00:19:43,633
I submitted evidence to the police
that I didn't order the murder.

214
00:19:43,633 --> 00:19:46,700
Then who is behind the assault?

215
00:19:47,600 --> 00:19:52,033
If I knew that, wouldn't I be the culprit?

216
00:19:57,567 --> 00:19:59,433
Madam! This way, over here!

217
00:19:59,433 --> 00:20:00,960
Move aside.

218
00:20:00,960 --> 00:20:03,968
- Please say something.
- Your statement.

219
00:20:03,968 --> 00:20:08,448
- Give us something.
- Any comment?

220
00:20:08,448 --> 00:20:11,864
- Please say something.
- Any comment.

221
00:20:12,467 --> 00:20:14,500
What happened, Madam?

222
00:20:14,500 --> 00:20:17,700
There was an urgent arrest.
I left after submitting the evidence.

223
00:20:17,700 --> 00:20:20,033
Where is my mother?

224
00:20:20,033 --> 00:20:23,167
She fled to the Philippines in a hurry.

225
00:20:25,333 --> 00:20:27,200
I must stop by somewhere.

226
00:20:27,200 --> 00:20:29,067
Yes, I'm sure you do.

227
00:20:29,067 --> 00:20:32,167
Madam, aren't you curious how I've been?

228
00:20:32,167 --> 00:20:34,967
I was held captive by Ga Seon Yeong
until I escaped moments ago!

229
00:20:34,967 --> 00:20:38,533
I nearly died for real.
Can't you see the state I'm in?

230
00:20:38,533 --> 00:20:40,600
But you're here safely now.

231
00:20:40,600 --> 00:20:42,667
Isn't that what matters?

232
00:20:42,667 --> 00:20:44,700
Madam,

233
00:20:44,700 --> 00:20:47,467
you're becoming more like
the chairman as time goes on.

234
00:20:47,467 --> 00:20:49,633
I'll take that as a compliment.

235
00:20:58,033 --> 00:21:02,433
<i>[Hoyang Trading Co.]</i>

236
00:21:19,467 --> 00:21:23,733
<i>You were investigated as the mastermind
behind Professor Ga Seon Yeong's assault, right?</i>

237
00:21:23,733 --> 00:21:27,600
<i>I submitted evidence to the police
that I didn't order the murder.</i>

238
00:21:27,600 --> 00:21:30,767
<i>Then who is behind the assault?</i>

239
00:21:30,767 --> 00:21:34,333
<i>If I knew that, wouldn't I be the culprit?</i>

240
00:21:34,333 --> 00:21:38,256
<i>- Please say something.
- Your statement.</i>

241
00:21:39,100 --> 00:21:40,867
Yes.

242
00:21:43,100 --> 00:21:45,133
Yes, what are you looking for?

243
00:21:46,833 --> 00:21:48,600
A ship heading to China.

244
00:21:48,600 --> 00:21:51,667
If you go straight along this big road,
you'll reach the terminal.

245
00:21:51,667 --> 00:21:53,500
Not that ship.

246
00:21:54,167 --> 00:21:56,000
How much would it cost?

247
00:21:58,800 --> 00:22:01,800
- You need at least ₩30 million.
- "Thirty million"?

248
00:22:02,567 --> 00:22:03,967
What? It costs that much?

249
00:22:03,967 --> 00:22:06,433
You came here without knowing market prices?

250
00:22:14,067 --> 00:22:15,800
If I pay, the ship leaves immediately, right?

251
00:22:15,800 --> 00:22:19,633
If you pay enough, it'll leave even in a typhoon.

252
00:22:25,833 --> 00:22:27,867
Come again.

253
00:22:50,400 --> 00:22:56,067
<i>Everything now depends on Vice President Ga Seon Woo.</i>

254
00:22:56,067 --> 00:22:58,467
<i>Please remember that.</i>

255
00:23:24,608 --> 00:23:26,867
<i>[Museum G]</i>

256
00:23:26,867 --> 00:23:29,100
"Museum G"?

257
00:23:33,300 --> 00:23:37,833
<i>[Museum G]</i>

258
00:23:39,867 --> 00:23:41,600
<i>[Museum G]</i>

259
00:23:44,800 --> 00:23:46,200
That's Ga Seon Yeong.

260
00:23:46,200 --> 00:23:48,600
<i>[Ga Seon Yeong, CEO of Museum G]</i>

261
00:23:51,633 --> 00:23:54,000
<i>[Ga Seon Yeong]</i>

262
00:23:54,000 --> 00:23:57,933
<i>[Ga Seon Yeong's Profile]</i>

263
00:23:59,267 --> 00:24:00,900
<i>[Ga Seon Yeong]</i>

264
00:24:02,667 --> 00:24:04,967
<i>[Key Activities: Volunteer Theater Therapy
for Prison Inmates Since 2008]</i>

265
00:24:09,767 --> 00:24:12,967
<i>[Ga Seon Yeong with Inmates]</i>

266
00:24:12,967 --> 00:24:15,633
<i>["Prisons Can Become Stages." Professor Ga Seon Yeong
does psychodrama at Cheongsan Prison.]</i>

267
00:24:20,367 --> 00:24:22,400
Isn't that Gil Ho Se?

268
00:24:31,967 --> 00:24:33,933
<i>[Gaseong Art Center, Professor Ga Seon Yeong
Reinterprets "Macbeth"]</i>

269
00:24:33,933 --> 00:24:36,300
<i>["Macbeth" to Run all October
at Gaseong Art Center]</i>

270
00:24:44,867 --> 00:24:47,600
<i>[Gaseong Art Center]</i>

271
00:24:47,600 --> 00:24:52,067
<i>[664 Seoho-daero, Gwangdong-gu, Seoul]</i>

272
00:24:52,067 --> 00:24:54,500
<i>[Golden Bridge Network]</i>

273
00:24:58,000 --> 00:24:59,700
Drink up.

274
00:25:02,567 --> 00:25:03,833
Thank you for the recording.

275
00:25:03,833 --> 00:25:05,433
It was tough.

276
00:25:05,433 --> 00:25:09,600
Gosh, your mom is really so suspicious.

277
00:25:13,833 --> 00:25:16,433
So how much do you want?

278
00:25:17,733 --> 00:25:22,233
You know jade is great for your health, right?

279
00:25:22,233 --> 00:25:26,667
Those are made with only top-grade jade beads.

280
00:25:26,667 --> 00:25:28,500
Please buy ten of those for me.

281
00:25:28,500 --> 00:25:30,533
It usually costs ₩500,000 ($350),

282
00:25:30,533 --> 00:25:35,267
but I'll give you a discount
and charge you only ₩300,000 each.

283
00:25:36,667 --> 00:25:38,467
Aunt Hyeon Ok,

284
00:25:39,333 --> 00:25:42,267
did you help me just to get such little money?

285
00:25:42,867 --> 00:25:47,800
Your mother's success is
the most gut-wrenching thing for me.

286
00:25:53,567 --> 00:25:55,400
Yeong Ran,

287
00:25:56,667 --> 00:26:02,767
I felt sorry for you
when you grew up getting beaten.

288
00:26:02,767 --> 00:26:05,133
I don't know what this fight is about,

289
00:26:05,133 --> 00:26:09,500
but now you have money and supporters.

290
00:26:09,500 --> 00:26:11,367
Make sure you win.

291
00:26:17,467 --> 00:26:19,200
I will.

292
00:26:23,067 --> 00:26:25,167
Oh my, oh my.

293
00:26:25,167 --> 00:26:27,400
Goodness.

294
00:26:28,667 --> 00:26:30,767
Madam, what's all this?

295
00:26:30,767 --> 00:26:34,000
Jade mats. Share them among yourselves.

296
00:26:34,000 --> 00:26:36,233
Thank you.

297
00:26:36,233 --> 00:26:38,033
Hey, Attorney Lee.

298
00:26:38,900 --> 00:26:42,233
Did Madam fully clear her charges?

299
00:26:42,233 --> 00:26:44,433
Her mom ordered it,
but how could the daughter not know?

300
00:26:44,433 --> 00:26:48,400
Butler Choi, I know that mother quite well.

301
00:26:48,400 --> 00:26:51,200
She's the type who would do it alone.

302
00:26:51,200 --> 00:26:53,767
Does that explain enough?

303
00:26:53,767 --> 00:26:56,967
Oh, let's have tofu stew for dinner,
as it's been a while,

304
00:26:56,967 --> 00:27:00,533
especially since someone here
just returned from the police station.

305
00:27:03,100 --> 00:27:05,233
What is it? Oh my!

306
00:27:05,233 --> 00:27:06,433
Oh my!

307
00:27:06,433 --> 00:27:07,733
They say this is good for your body.

308
00:27:07,733 --> 00:27:09,367
I guess I need to lay two of these in my room.

309
00:27:09,367 --> 00:27:10,500
You need to lie on it.

310
00:27:10,500 --> 00:27:14,000
"She seduced a 70-year-old man
and is now trying to kill his daughter."

311
00:27:14,000 --> 00:27:16,233
You've become quite the famous widow.

312
00:27:16,233 --> 00:27:19,300
At this rate, you'll be
more famous than the president.

313
00:27:21,633 --> 00:27:23,967
That slipped out unknowingly.

314
00:27:23,967 --> 00:27:25,367
One thing's for sure.

315
00:27:25,367 --> 00:27:29,167
Ga Seon Yeong still hasn't secured that video.

316
00:27:29,167 --> 00:27:31,933
She probably blocked all of
Ga Seon Woo's money sources.

317
00:27:31,933 --> 00:27:36,200
Yes, blocked his credit cards
and put him on the no-fly list, right?

318
00:27:37,133 --> 00:27:38,167
<i>[Caller ID Restricted]</i>

319
00:27:39,767 --> 00:27:41,500
Ga Seon Woo?

320
00:27:45,333 --> 00:27:47,100
Yes, this is Lee Don.

321
00:27:47,100 --> 00:27:51,600
Attorney Lee, are you with Kim Yeong Ran now?

322
00:27:51,600 --> 00:27:54,967
Put her on. I need to talk.

323
00:27:56,167 --> 00:27:59,333
He wants to speak with you directly, Madam.

324
00:28:03,200 --> 00:28:05,133
<i>[Caller ID Restricted]</i>

325
00:28:05,133 --> 00:28:06,533
Kim Yeong Ran speaking.

326
00:28:06,533 --> 00:28:08,733
Hey, Kim Yeong Ran,

327
00:28:08,733 --> 00:28:12,267
what the heck do you want from me? What?

328
00:28:12,267 --> 00:28:14,833
And why are you saying those things to reporters?

329
00:28:14,833 --> 00:28:18,567
You claimed to have a video
to take down Ga Seon Yeong, right?

330
00:28:18,567 --> 00:28:19,967
How did you know that?

331
00:28:19,967 --> 00:28:22,467
<i>With that, we can fully crush Ga Seon Yeong.</i>

332
00:28:22,467 --> 00:28:24,633
Just stay out of Korea until things calm down.

333
00:28:24,633 --> 00:28:27,267
Not a bad offer, is it? Think about it.

334
00:28:27,267 --> 00:28:28,900
<i>[Caller ID Restricted]</i>

335
00:28:28,900 --> 00:28:31,533
How can you hang up like this, Madam?

336
00:28:31,533 --> 00:28:35,700
The fact that he contacted us like this
means he's surely cornered.

337
00:28:35,700 --> 00:28:37,933
He will surely call again.

338
00:28:49,133 --> 00:28:51,833
Jeez, this is a mess!

339
00:29:11,600 --> 00:29:12,700
<i>[Caller ID Restricted]</i>

340
00:29:22,333 --> 00:29:23,900
<i>But I have conditions, too.</i>

341
00:29:23,900 --> 00:29:26,600
Deposit ₩10 billion ($7 million)
into an untraceable account,

342
00:29:26,600 --> 00:29:30,700
and bring ₩300 million in cash
to Pyeongtan Port dock by 9 p.m. tonight.

343
00:29:30,700 --> 00:29:33,467
Don't even dream of doing something stupid.

344
00:29:39,833 --> 00:29:43,233
What are those two doing in there?

345
00:29:44,300 --> 00:29:46,533
What do you mean?

346
00:29:46,533 --> 00:29:48,700
Butler Jo,

347
00:29:48,700 --> 00:29:52,700
don't you think Madam and Attorney Lee
are acting suspicious?

348
00:29:52,700 --> 00:29:55,000
Suspicious how?

349
00:29:55,000 --> 00:29:58,267
Her elderly husband just died,

350
00:29:58,267 --> 00:30:02,600
and she's been shut in the study
with a young lawyer for two hours.

351
00:30:02,600 --> 00:30:04,700
Doesn't that seem odd to you, Butler Jo?

352
00:30:05,400 --> 00:30:09,533
Butler Choi, you haven't had
much experience with romance, have you?

353
00:30:09,533 --> 00:30:12,133
I was quite popular back in the day. Why?

354
00:30:12,133 --> 00:30:16,867
Does Yeong Ran look at the attorney
like someone in love?

355
00:30:16,867 --> 00:30:19,633
Who knows what's in her heart?

356
00:30:19,633 --> 00:30:23,133
One thing is for sure. It's not the attorney.

357
00:30:23,133 --> 00:30:27,033
Those two act indifferent to each other,

358
00:30:27,033 --> 00:30:28,933
just like us.

359
00:30:29,933 --> 00:30:31,700
What does that mean?

360
00:30:31,700 --> 00:30:34,367
It's strangely convincing.

361
00:30:36,500 --> 00:30:40,300
Gosh, why is it so dirty? Full of dust.

362
00:30:40,300 --> 00:30:43,300
Oh! Madam, you were here?

363
00:30:44,067 --> 00:30:46,333
They say couples resemble each other.

364
00:30:46,333 --> 00:30:49,233
She becomes just like
the late Chairman Ga Sung Ho.

365
00:30:54,433 --> 00:30:57,467
Why do I hear water here?

366
00:31:07,700 --> 00:31:10,367
That's odd.

367
00:31:13,333 --> 00:31:16,467
So peculiar.

368
00:31:18,300 --> 00:31:21,400
<i>[Macbeth, Gaseong Art Center]</i>

369
00:31:43,500 --> 00:31:48,233
<i>[Gaseong Art Center]</i>

370
00:31:49,633 --> 00:31:54,933
<i>[Macbeth, Gaseong Art Center]</i>

371
00:32:03,700 --> 00:32:06,167
Hyung, did you check what I asked?

372
00:32:06,167 --> 00:32:09,400
But according to this, it's not Gil Ho Se.

373
00:32:09,400 --> 00:32:10,830
It's a guy named Gil Tae
<i>[Inmate Identity Card]</i>

374
00:32:10,830 --> 00:32:13,433
who got 10 years
for parricide and arson as a teen

375
00:32:13,433 --> 00:32:15,733
and served time at Cheongsan Prison.

376
00:32:15,733 --> 00:32:19,300
- I think this might be the same person as Gil Ho Se.
- Are you sure?

377
00:32:19,300 --> 00:32:22,200
<i>But why did you ask me to search for this?</i>

378
00:32:22,200 --> 00:32:25,000
- I need to check something.
- <i>Don't tell me, you're...</i>

379
00:32:25,000 --> 00:32:28,633
Are you personally investigating since
Gil Ho Se's investigation is blocked?

380
00:32:28,633 --> 00:32:32,767
- It's not like that.
- Hey, don't do anything unnecessary. Got it, Jeon Dong Min?

381
00:32:32,767 --> 00:32:34,967
<i>Yes, I'll call you later.</i>

382
00:32:59,167 --> 00:33:03,433
<i>[Grand Theater]</i>

383
00:33:32,660 --> 00:33:34,600
Gil Ho Se?

384
00:33:39,530 --> 00:33:44,233
Right then messengers from His Majesty arrived.

385
00:33:57,533 --> 00:34:00,033
<i>If you reject my offer,</i>

386
00:34:00,567 --> 00:34:02,800
<i>I'll send this to Kim Yeong Ran.</i>

387
00:34:02,800 --> 00:34:04,700
<i>Do whatever you want.</i>

388
00:34:05,933 --> 00:34:07,967
Seon Woo

389
00:34:09,833 --> 00:34:13,767
has the video from the day Ye Rim died.

390
00:34:15,033 --> 00:34:17,167
Is he blackmailing you with that?

391
00:34:17,167 --> 00:34:20,367
He wants me to abandon all I've built.

392
00:34:22,200 --> 00:34:27,667
Just when I'm about to take over Gaseong Group,
the company my mother founded.

393
00:34:35,067 --> 00:34:38,333
You know how badly I want that, right?

394
00:34:39,267 --> 00:34:40,967
Professor.

395
00:34:41,900 --> 00:34:44,267
What can I do?

396
00:35:01,730 --> 00:35:05,067
<i>[27 Pyeongtan Haenam-ro, Haean-gu, Pyeongtan City]</i>

397
00:35:58,700 --> 00:36:00,967
I brought ₩30 million.

398
00:36:00,967 --> 00:36:03,733
Get me a boat leaving tonight.

399
00:36:03,733 --> 00:36:06,200
Tonight is too soon.

400
00:36:06,200 --> 00:36:08,833
Tell them I'll give as much money as they want.

401
00:36:08,833 --> 00:36:11,133
I'll try to arrange it.

402
00:36:11,133 --> 00:36:13,900
Do people work here

403
00:36:13,900 --> 00:36:16,500
at the dock even at night?

404
00:36:16,500 --> 00:36:19,500
These days, no one works due to the strike.

405
00:36:19,500 --> 00:36:21,567
But why do you ask?

406
00:36:22,267 --> 00:36:23,933
It's no big deal.

407
00:36:40,167 --> 00:36:43,467
The person you're looking for just arrived.

408
00:37:24,733 --> 00:37:26,467
It's 128 Hanseo-dong.

409
00:37:26,467 --> 00:37:30,133
Reporters are crowding the area
and blocking traffic.

410
00:37:30,133 --> 00:37:32,833
Please take care of the situation onsite.

411
00:37:45,533 --> 00:37:47,200
<i>[Mad Dog]</i>

412
00:37:47,200 --> 00:37:49,333
- What's going on?
- Don.

413
00:37:49,333 --> 00:37:51,467
Where is Yeong Ran right now?

414
00:37:51,467 --> 00:37:53,500
She's not Yeong Ran; she is Madam now.

415
00:37:53,500 --> 00:37:56,433
I appreciate your help until now.

416
00:37:56,433 --> 00:37:59,867
If you need money, text me.
Just don't cause trouble.

417
00:38:27,900 --> 00:38:30,600
Oh Lord, please.
<i>[Curriculum and Methods for Early Childhood Education]</i>

418
00:38:30,600 --> 00:38:34,767
Please grant this one a score of 60.

419
00:38:38,000 --> 00:38:39,933
Let's do this.

420
00:38:42,333 --> 00:38:43,700
Okay.

421
00:38:43,700 --> 00:38:45,600
Oh my.

422
00:38:46,333 --> 00:38:48,233
What brings you here, Ms. Kim Se Rang?

423
00:38:48,233 --> 00:38:51,833
Principal, it's pickup time.
Parents will arrive soon.

424
00:38:51,833 --> 00:38:54,100
Oh dear, it's this late already.

425
00:38:54,100 --> 00:38:55,733
My class...

426
00:38:55,733 --> 00:38:58,033
How was the class?

427
00:38:58,033 --> 00:39:01,000
And they said a driver
will be available next week.

428
00:39:01,000 --> 00:39:03,000
Things should improve for us, too.

429
00:39:03,000 --> 00:39:04,367
Let's go, let's go.

430
00:39:04,367 --> 00:39:08,367
<i>What's this about hiring unqualified
kindergarten teachers illegally?</i>

431
00:39:08,367 --> 00:39:12,533
<i>- Principal Lee Mi Seon must explain!</i>
- Here we go again, Kang Seong Tae.

432
00:39:12,533 --> 00:39:15,900
- Principal, did you really hire someone illegally?
- N-No, that's...

433
00:39:15,900 --> 00:39:18,133
If the education office finds out,
the kindergarten will close!

434
00:39:18,133 --> 00:39:19,533
Oh Lord, now...

435
00:39:19,533 --> 00:39:22,767
Miss, please report this to the police first.

436
00:39:22,767 --> 00:39:24,967
But Principal, I think this should be reported

437
00:39:24,967 --> 00:39:26,933
to the education office, not the police.

438
00:39:26,933 --> 00:39:29,400
Whose side are you on?

439
00:39:29,400 --> 00:39:31,900
On the side of justice!

440
00:39:31,900 --> 00:39:34,000
Please stay here and do nothing!

441
00:39:34,000 --> 00:39:37,267
I beg you in the name of justice!

442
00:39:37,267 --> 00:39:41,633
What's this about hiring unqualified
kindergarten teachers illegally?

443
00:39:41,633 --> 00:39:43,833
What is this? What is this?

444
00:39:43,833 --> 00:39:48,133
Muchang Iseon Kindergarten Principal Lee Mi Seon
must explain now!

445
00:39:48,133 --> 00:39:50,233
Explain yourself! Explain!

446
00:39:50,233 --> 00:39:52,633
Ms. Jenny, please call the police.

447
00:39:52,633 --> 00:39:56,333
- What?
- Kang Seong Tae, let's settle this today!

448
00:39:56,333 --> 00:39:59,167
Fine, let's settle this!

449
00:40:00,700 --> 00:40:01,600
Jeong Hwa!

450
00:40:01,600 --> 00:40:02,933
When will you grow up?

451
00:40:02,933 --> 00:40:05,367
This is the kindergarten my daughter goes to!

452
00:40:05,367 --> 00:40:07,533
That's exactly why I'm doing this.

453
00:40:07,533 --> 00:40:09,233
Falsifying credentials and an illegal hiring

454
00:40:09,233 --> 00:40:12,667
at a kindergarten that teaches children,
does that make sense?

455
00:40:12,667 --> 00:40:16,100
That gold digger Bu Se Mi,
or whatever her name is!

456
00:40:16,100 --> 00:40:18,067
We have a new teacher now!

457
00:40:18,067 --> 00:40:20,033
Hae Na will keep attending this kindergarten

458
00:40:20,033 --> 00:40:23,033
so stop this nonsense.

459
00:40:23,033 --> 00:40:26,967
For the children's bright future and Muchang's endless development—

460
00:40:26,967 --> 00:40:31,300
Even Annoah, Dong Min's dog, knows you're
after the kindergarten's land!

461
00:40:31,300 --> 00:40:33,800
Kang Seong Tae, get your life together first.

462
00:40:33,800 --> 00:40:35,133
Principal, we will be going now.

463
00:40:35,133 --> 00:40:36,533
- Yes, Ma'am.
- Say goodbye, Hae Na.

464
00:40:36,533 --> 00:40:39,000
Goodbye.

465
00:40:39,000 --> 00:40:40,833
Jeong Hwa.

466
00:40:42,200 --> 00:40:46,167
Hey! You're banned from our market!

467
00:40:46,167 --> 00:40:49,333
No, no, no! Don't do this!

468
00:40:49,333 --> 00:40:51,333
Don't follow us!

469
00:40:51,333 --> 00:40:55,167
- No, that's not it!
- Oh, gosh.

470
00:40:55,167 --> 00:40:58,267
Our beloved Ms. Bu Se Mi,

471
00:40:58,267 --> 00:41:03,500
where are you? I miss you so much.

472
00:41:06,800 --> 00:41:11,800
Muchang must be noisy again from Seong Tae.

473
00:41:13,800 --> 00:41:17,767
Come to think of it, autumn has come to Muchang.

474
00:41:17,767 --> 00:41:20,867
The autumn leaves in Muchang are very beautiful.

475
00:41:20,867 --> 00:41:22,800
Like you, Hye Ji.

476
00:41:24,600 --> 00:41:31,167
Hye Ji, I hope you wake soon. We can go see it together.

477
00:41:37,060 --> 00:41:39,233
The IV drip has run out.

478
00:41:42,430 --> 00:41:44,467
<i>Doctor.</i>

479
00:43:02,230 --> 00:43:06,100
<i>Oh! You're here.</i>

480
00:43:09,330 --> 00:43:10,933
Is it him?

481
00:43:13,860 --> 00:43:18,467
If you give me one more bill,
I think I'll remember for sure.

482
00:43:34,460 --> 00:43:37,400
Yes, that's correct. It's definitely him.

483
00:43:37,400 --> 00:43:41,800
He asked me to find a boat to China tonight.

484
00:43:47,733 --> 00:43:49,867
Is that all?

485
00:43:53,760 --> 00:44:00,167
He asked if many people work at the dock even at night.

486
00:44:24,360 --> 00:44:27,000
<i>[Restroom]</i>

487
00:45:33,830 --> 00:45:36,233
It's sector B-1.

488
00:45:53,060 --> 00:45:58,400
Madam, the CCTV isn't working due to the strike
so it might be dangerous.

489
00:45:58,400 --> 00:46:01,033
If Ga Seon Woo does anything suspicious,
contact me instantly.

490
00:46:01,033 --> 00:46:04,367
I'll wait here.

491
00:46:05,600 --> 00:46:07,500
I'll be back.

492
00:46:14,660 --> 00:46:18,367
<i>[We will never tolerate exploitation at the ports!]</i>

493
00:46:36,200 --> 00:46:37,933
<i>[Mad Dog]</i>

494
00:46:39,260 --> 00:46:41,600
Didn't I tell you to text me?

495
00:46:41,600 --> 00:46:43,333
Just hear me out first.

496
00:46:43,333 --> 00:46:46,100
I'm tailing Gil Ho Se, but something feels off.

497
00:46:46,100 --> 00:46:49,667
What? Why are you chasing Gil Ho Se?

498
00:46:54,330 --> 00:46:55,700
Are you at Pyeongtan Port?

499
00:46:55,700 --> 00:46:57,733
Are you at Pyeongtan Port, too?

500
00:47:00,430 --> 00:47:03,700
<i>Jeon Dong Min, just stay put.</i>

501
00:47:52,930 --> 00:47:56,800
It's been a while, Kim Yeong Ran.

502
00:48:09,300 --> 00:48:10,933
Don.

503
00:48:20,500 --> 00:48:22,167
You verified it, right?

504
00:48:23,160 --> 00:48:24,767
Give me the money.

505
00:48:29,160 --> 00:48:30,800
Hold on.

506
00:48:31,660 --> 00:48:35,233
How can I trust that evidence is real?

507
00:48:38,930 --> 00:48:41,533
It's real, okay?

508
00:48:41,533 --> 00:48:43,633
It's real so trust me, darn it!

509
00:48:43,633 --> 00:48:46,367
Would I lie in this situation?

510
00:48:48,200 --> 00:48:52,233
Everything my sister did is in here.

511
00:48:53,300 --> 00:48:56,800
So please, just trust me.

512
00:48:59,260 --> 00:49:01,967
Are you going to do it or not?

513
00:49:04,760 --> 00:49:07,800
Darn it, I'm losing it here.

514
00:49:20,360 --> 00:49:24,433
You'd better be careful, too, Kim Yeong Ran.

515
00:50:39,700 --> 00:50:41,400
Madam.

516
00:50:59,467 --> 00:51:01,733
Who put you up to this?

517
00:51:01,733 --> 00:51:03,967
Was it Ga Seon Yeong? Right?

518
00:51:03,967 --> 00:51:06,433
How could she kill her own brother?

519
00:51:09,567 --> 00:51:11,467
What's so funny?

520
00:51:11,467 --> 00:51:13,633
What is so funny?

521
00:51:13,633 --> 00:51:15,800
You're all insane!

522
00:51:16,600 --> 00:51:18,100
What are you doing?

523
00:51:18,100 --> 00:51:20,533
Don't do it! Don't!

524
00:51:20,533 --> 00:51:22,767
Stop!

525
00:51:43,867 --> 00:51:45,700
Yeong Ran!

526
00:51:51,067 --> 00:51:52,733
Yeong Ran,

527
00:51:52,733 --> 00:51:54,367
are you okay?

528
00:51:55,900 --> 00:51:57,900
Why are you here, Dong Min?

529
00:51:57,900 --> 00:52:01,300
I followed Gil Ho Se.

530
00:52:02,733 --> 00:52:05,633
Madam! Are you all right?

531
00:52:07,100 --> 00:52:08,733
Madam.

532
00:52:10,133 --> 00:52:12,000
What is happening here?

533
00:52:12,000 --> 00:52:15,333
Gil Ho Se killed Ga Seon Woo
and committed suicide.

534
00:52:15,333 --> 00:52:16,767
What?

535
00:52:20,133 --> 00:52:22,000
Did someone call the cops?

536
00:52:22,000 --> 00:52:23,800
Wait.

537
00:52:23,800 --> 00:52:26,300
This is a trap set by Ga Seon Yeong.

538
00:52:27,667 --> 00:52:30,533
Madam, give that to me.

539
00:52:39,467 --> 00:52:41,567
Quickly, get out of here.

540
00:52:58,667 --> 00:53:00,300
We seem already surrounded.

541
00:53:00,300 --> 00:53:03,900
You two go ahead.
I'll stay behind and try to handle it.

542
00:53:03,900 --> 00:53:05,067
What do you mean?

543
00:53:05,067 --> 00:53:08,133
Ms. Yeong Ran, if you get involved,
it will complicate things more.

544
00:53:08,133 --> 00:53:10,567
Please listen to me, okay?

545
00:53:11,500 --> 00:53:12,433
Go quickly.

546
00:53:12,433 --> 00:53:14,900
- Dong Min.
- Hurry!

547
00:53:14,900 --> 00:53:17,967
No. We can't leave you here alone.

548
00:53:17,967 --> 00:53:19,067
No.

549
00:53:19,067 --> 00:53:22,200
Wait, Madam. Dong Min is right.

550
00:53:22,200 --> 00:53:26,467
If you get arrested,
all we built will go down the drain!

551
00:53:26,467 --> 00:53:28,367
Let's go!

552
00:53:28,367 --> 00:53:30,667
What does that mean?

553
00:53:30,667 --> 00:53:33,700
If we stay, all three of us
will get caught, Madam!

554
00:53:34,900 --> 00:53:38,467
Dong Min is also my brother.

555
00:53:38,467 --> 00:53:42,733
You need to leave so we can save Dong Min!

556
00:53:42,733 --> 00:53:46,200
No, I'll get him out no matter what.

557
00:53:46,200 --> 00:53:48,367
Let's go, Madam!

558
00:54:01,700 --> 00:54:05,267
It's okay, Yeong Ran. Don't worry.

559
00:54:15,200 --> 00:54:17,900
I'll surely come to save you.

560
00:54:17,900 --> 00:54:20,233
Dong Min, I'm so sorry.

561
00:54:21,067 --> 00:54:22,733
Just go.

562
00:54:24,067 --> 00:54:25,570
Hurry.

563
00:54:26,267 --> 00:54:28,067
Let's go.

564
00:54:28,067 --> 00:54:29,967
Madam, let's go.

565
00:55:01,400 --> 00:55:03,600
Drop the gun and put your hands up!

566
00:55:04,967 --> 00:55:07,200
Please just go.

567
00:55:10,433 --> 00:55:11,633
Drop the gun!

568
00:55:11,633 --> 00:55:13,767
Put your hands above your head.

569
00:56:06,500 --> 00:56:12,767
The autopsy results show cause of death
was head trauma from a gunshot.

570
00:56:15,767 --> 00:56:17,633
Who is the perpetrator?

571
00:56:17,633 --> 00:56:21,333
The suspect was caught at the scene
and is currently being transported to Seoul.

572
00:56:30,033 --> 00:56:31,967
The USB was completely destroyed,

573
00:56:31,967 --> 00:56:34,933
and Ho Se committed suicide there.

574
00:56:34,933 --> 00:56:36,333
What about Ho Se's body?

575
00:56:36,333 --> 00:56:38,370
There was nothing to verify his identity.

576
00:56:38,370 --> 00:56:41,560
He was sent to a morgue for unclaimed bodies.

577
00:56:42,633 --> 00:56:44,500
He was quite useful, though.

578
00:56:44,500 --> 00:56:47,133
Kim Yeong Ran and Lee Don fled immediately,

579
00:56:47,133 --> 00:56:51,033
and a suspect named Jeon Dong Min
was arrested at the scene.

580
00:56:52,633 --> 00:56:54,633
"Jeon Dong Min"?

581
00:57:04,267 --> 00:57:06,067
Interesting.

582
00:57:11,433 --> 00:57:15,133
Oh my, Yeong Ran! What on Earth is happening?

583
00:57:24,767 --> 00:57:27,133
The situation got complicated,

584
00:57:27,133 --> 00:57:31,267
but I'll find evidence somehow
and get Dong Min out.

585
00:57:31,267 --> 00:57:34,800
First, let's check
which police station he went to.

586
00:57:34,800 --> 00:57:38,500
Madam, you need to stay alert,
especially in times like this.

587
00:57:38,500 --> 00:57:40,633
Do you understand?

588
00:57:40,633 --> 00:57:43,767
- Please take good care of Madam.
- Oh, yes.

589
00:57:45,633 --> 00:57:48,100
Yeong Ran, I'll bring you some water.

590
00:57:59,567 --> 00:58:01,600
<i>[Ga Seon Yeong]</i>

591
00:58:03,233 --> 00:58:05,700
<i>If you want to save Jeon Dong Min,</i>

592
00:58:05,700 --> 00:58:07,733
come find me yourself.

593
00:58:10,967 --> 00:58:13,233
<i>[Ga Seon Yeong]</i>

594
00:58:13,233 --> 00:58:16,633
<i>[Why did Mr. Jeon, who sold strawberries to
Chairman Ga, kill Gaseong Group's VP?]</i>

595
00:58:49,700 --> 00:58:52,800
What the heck are you up to now?

596
00:58:52,800 --> 00:58:54,633
Wait.

597
00:58:55,867 --> 00:58:59,133
Could you pick a photo for the article?

598
00:58:59,133 --> 00:59:02,900
They all look good so it's hard to choose.

599
00:59:04,833 --> 00:59:09,167
By 9 a.m. tomorrow,
Dong Min's face will be everywhere.

600
00:59:10,100 --> 00:59:12,500
Stop this now, Ga Seon Yeong.

601
00:59:16,633 --> 00:59:19,800
Jeon Dong Min's son's name is Jeon Ju Won, right?

602
00:59:23,267 --> 00:59:25,200
He's cute.

603
00:59:27,600 --> 00:59:31,700
Jeon Dong Min grew up parentless, raised by his cousin.

604
00:59:31,700 --> 00:59:34,533
What if his son grows up like that, too?

605
00:59:34,533 --> 00:59:37,967
Being pointed at as a murderer's son.

606
00:59:41,733 --> 00:59:44,100
Are you even human after all this?

607
00:59:49,833 --> 00:59:53,300
<i>[Suicide Note, Kim Yeong Ran]</i>

608
00:59:53,300 --> 00:59:56,500
I'll show mercy one last time.

609
00:59:57,833 --> 01:00:00,267
To stop this article,

610
01:00:04,467 --> 01:00:07,300
you just have to die, Kim Yeong Ran.

611
01:00:10,633 --> 01:00:15,000
"I killed Ga Seon Woo. I didn't want to
split Chairman Ga Sung Ho's inheritance."

612
01:00:15,967 --> 01:00:18,733
"And I also tried to kill Ga Seon Yeong."

613
01:00:18,733 --> 01:00:23,167
"I never meant for things to go this far.
I'll atone through death and find freedom."

614
01:00:23,167 --> 01:00:24,700
How about it?

615
01:00:30,733 --> 01:00:34,900
As long as you die,
I won't release Dong Min's photo nationwide.

616
01:00:39,933 --> 01:00:41,633
Ga Seon Yeong.

617
01:00:46,833 --> 01:00:48,833
If you don't like it, kill me.

618
01:00:49,700 --> 01:00:54,116
Kill me and frame this innocent man
as the criminal.

619
01:00:54,116 --> 01:00:55,500
Darn you!

620
01:00:55,500 --> 01:00:57,133
Kill me.

621
01:00:58,833 --> 01:01:01,100
- Let go.
- Just kill me instead!

622
01:02:17,433 --> 01:02:20,233
<i>I'll surely come to save you.</i>

623
01:02:20,233 --> 01:02:21,867
<i>Hurry up and go.</i>

624
01:02:26,733 --> 01:02:30,100
<i>I never should have gone to Muchang.</i>

625
01:02:33,400 --> 01:02:36,067
Then none of this would have happened.

626
01:02:38,767 --> 01:02:41,100
I ruined everything.

627
01:02:44,767 --> 01:02:47,767
I thought money was the most important thing,

628
01:02:48,567 --> 01:02:50,700
but I was wrong.

629
01:02:55,333 --> 01:02:58,067
<i>[Suicide Note]</i>

630
01:03:05,033 --> 01:03:07,867
I'll put an end to all of this now.

631
01:03:13,533 --> 01:03:17,233
I'm sorry, Chairman.

632
01:04:15,100 --> 01:04:19,833
After all this, you want to quit everything and die?

633
01:04:32,133 --> 01:04:33,900
Chairman?

634
01:04:43,610 --> 01:04:46,480
🤫<i>Ms. Incognito</i>🎭

635
01:04:46,480 --> 01:04:56,590
<i>Timing and subtitles by the</i> 👠 Se Mi Secrets 🕶️ <i>Team @viki.com</i>

636
01:05:27,267 --> 01:05:30,667
<i>I'll now reveal
the late Chairman Ga Sung Ho's will.</i>

637
01:05:30,667 --> 01:05:32,600
<i>You should have stopped her
even if it meant killing her!</i>

638
01:05:32,600 --> 01:05:34,600
<i>Wipe him clean from the Seon Woo case.</i>

639
01:05:34,600 --> 01:05:36,200
<i>What should we do about these two?</i>

640
01:05:36,200 --> 01:05:38,400
<i>Prosecutor Kim,
write a good script for this case.</i>

641
01:05:38,400 --> 01:05:40,200
<i>We will take over this case.
[Pyeongtan Port: Death Incident Report]</i>

642
01:05:40,200 --> 01:05:41,133
<i>- Let go.
- Hey!</i>

643
01:05:41,133 --> 01:05:45,800
<i>Turn off all the house cameras
and evacuate everyone from the main building?</i>

644
01:05:45,800 --> 01:05:46,967
<i>Byeol Nae, is something wrong?</i>

645
01:05:46,967 --> 01:05:50,300
<i>Yeong Ran, someone came to the house.</i>

646
01:05:50,300 --> 01:05:52,200
<i>Ga Seon Yeong came.</i>

647
01:05:52,200 --> 01:05:54,080
<i>Ga Seon Yeong came to the house.</i>

648
01:05:54,080 --> 01:05:58,730
♫ <i>Cause I was</i> ♫

